  "hints": [
    "You'll need to clean the status field by removing whitespace and normalizing case before using it in comparisons.",
    "Use SPLIT_PART to extract the first amount from the comma-separated schedule, COALESCE to replace NULL missed_count with 0, and a CASE expression to assign the late penalty based on the cleaned status.",
    "The solution is: SELECT plan_id, customer_email, INITCAP(TRIM(plan_status)) AS clean_status, SPLIT_PART(payment_schedule, ',', 1) AS next_payment_amount, 100 - (COALESCE(missed_count, 0) * 15) - (CASE WHEN LOWER(TRIM(plan_status)) = 'overdue' THEN 10 WHEN LOWER(TRIM(plan_status)) = 'warning' THEN 5 ELSE 0 END) AS health_score FROM payment_plans ORDER BY health_score DESC, plan_id;"
  ],
  "answer_key": "SELECT plan_id, customer_email, INITCAP(TRIM(plan_status)) AS clean_status, SPLIT_PART(payment_schedule, ',', 1) AS next_payment_amount, 100 - (COALESCE(missed_count, 0) * 15) - (CASE WHEN LOWER(TRIM(plan_status)) = 'overdue' THEN 10 WHEN LOWER(TRIM(plan_status)) = 'warning' THEN 5 ELSE 0 END) AS health_score FROM payment_plans ORDER BY health_score DESC, plan_id;",
